pkg-be is a pkg(8) plugin that creates a ZFS boot environment before
pkg upgrades (and, optionally, installs, deletes and autoremoves).
If an update breaks the system, the previous state can be booted again.

It keeps only the newest boot environments (by count and/or age),
records which packages changed as ZFS user properties, and adds a
"pkg be" command to list, compare and roll back boot environments.
